===Chile vs Italy===
{{Main|Battle of Santiago (1962 FIFA World Cup)}}
The game was tough with much foul play. After only seven minutes Ferrini was sent off for kicking Landa and the game had to be interrupted for another eight minutes until the police escorted the Italian out of the field. Soon afterwards [[Leonel Sánchez]] responded to a series of kicks from [[Mario David (footballer)|Mario David]] by knocking him down with a punch in front of the linesman. The referee did nothing so David took revenge on Sánchez before halftime and was also sent off. Italians held out in the second half until [[Jaime Ramírez (footballer, born 1931)|Jaime Ramírez]] headed the ball into the net over two defenders after Sánchez's shot was punched away by [[Carlo Mattrel]]. In the last minutes [[Jorge Toro]] secured the Chilean victory with a long-range shot.<ref name="lingua" /><ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5rZqRouIHJ0&t Chile vs Italy on YouTube]</ref>

